fullDescription.text:
Reports uses of primitive 'sync/atomic' functions, such as 'atomic.AddInt64' and 'atomic.LoadInt64', that can be replaced with typed atomic values. Typed atomic values, such as 'atomic.Int64', make atomic access part of the field type. This helps prevent non-atomic access to the same value and avoids alignment problems on 32-bit platforms. Example: 'type Counter struct {
	hits int64
}

func (c *Counter) Bump() {
	atomic.AddInt64(&c.hits, 1)
}

func (c *Counter) Read() int64 {
	return atomic.LoadInt64(&c.hits)
}' To fix the code, use the Replace int64 by atomic.Int64 quick-fix. After the quick-fix is applied: 'type Counter struct {
	hits atomic.Int64
}

func (c *Counter) Bump() {
	c.hits.Add(1)
}

func (c *Counter) Read() int64 {
	return c.hits.Load()
}' Inspection ID: GoFixAtomicTypes

fullDescription.markdown:
