Reports calls to 'errors.As' that can be replaced with 'errors.AsType'. In Go 1.26 and later, 'errors.AsType[T]' returns the matched error value directly. This removes the separately declared variable and the pointer passed to 'errors.As'. Example: 'func Describe(err error) string {
	var pe *PathError
	if errors.As(err, &pe) {
		return fmt.Sprintf("path error during %s", pe.Op)
	}
	return "other"
}' To fix the code, use the Replace errors.As with AsType[*PathError] quick-fix. After the quick-fix is applied: 'func Describe(err error) string {
	if pe, ok := errors.AsType[*PathError](err); ok {
		return fmt.Sprintf("path error during %s", pe.Op)
	}
	return "other"
}' Inspection ID: GoFixErrorsAsType

